<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!DOCTYPE refentry PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DocBook XML V4.2//EN"
   "http://www.oasis-open.org/docbook/xml/4.2/docbookx.dtd">
<refentry id="odfview">
  <refentryinfo>
    <productname>odfpy</productname>
  </refentryinfo>
  <refmeta>
    <refentrytitle>odfview</refentrytitle>
    <manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
    <refmiscinfo class="manual">User commands</refmiscinfo>
  </refmeta>

<refnamediv>
<refname>odfview</refname>
<refpurpose>Export a partial spreadsheet view for a selected set of tracked
row/column changes</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<cmdsynopsis>
    <command>odfview</command>
    <arg rep="repeat">-c <replaceable>change-id</replaceable></arg>
    <arg>-a</arg>
    <arg>-l</arg>
    <arg choice="opt">-t <replaceable>table</replaceable></arg>
    <arg choice="opt">-o <replaceable>csv-path</replaceable></arg>
    <arg choice="opt">-u <replaceable>unresolvable-csv</replaceable></arg>
    <arg choice="plain"><replaceable>spreadsheet.ods</replaceable></arg>
</cmdsynopsis>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsect1><title>Description</title>
<para><command>odfview</command> reads the unresolved table change records
(row/column insertions, deletions and movements) stored in an OpenDocument
spreadsheet and rebuilds the sheet as it would look if only the changes
selected on the command line were applied.
</para>
<para>
A selected change is kept <emphasis>applied</emphasis>. The empty selection
therefore reconstructs the original sheet: inserted rows/columns disappear,
deleted rows/columns (including their saved old values) come back, and
movements are undone. Selecting every change reproduces the current sheet.
</para>
<para>
A change that depends on another change (for example a movement that moves
rows created by an earlier insertion) cannot be rebuilt when the prerequisite
is not selected. The cells covered by such a change are written to the
unresolvable report instead of receiving invented coordinates; all unrelated
areas of the sheet are still exported normally.
</para>
</refsect1>

<refsect1><title>Options</title>
<variablelist>

<varlistentry>
<term>-c <replaceable>change-id</replaceable></term>
<listitem>
<para>
Keep the tracked change with this identifier applied. The option may be
repeated to select several changes. Use <option>-l</option> to discover the
identifiers present in the document.
</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term>-a</term>
<listitem>
<para>
Select every tracked change, reproducing the current sheet.
</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term>-l</term>
<listitem>
<para>
List the tracked changes (identifier, kind, position and dependencies) and
exit without exporting a view.
</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term>-t <replaceable>table</replaceable></term>
<listitem>
<para>
Table to export, given by name or zero based index. Defaults to the first
table.
</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term>-o <replaceable>csv-path</replaceable></term>
<listitem>
<para>
Write the reconstructed view as CSV to this file. Defaults to standard output.
</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term>-u <replaceable>unresolvable-csv</replaceable></term>
<listitem>
<para>
Write the cells that cannot be rebuilt for the selection to this CSV file.
Defaults to standard error.
</para>
</listitem>
</varlistentry>

</variablelist>
</refsect1>

<refsect1><title>Examples</title>
<screen>
odfview -l accounts.ods
odfview -c ctm-1 -c ctm-2 -o view.csv -u broken.csv accounts.ods
odfview -a accounts.ods
</screen>
</refsect1>

<refsect1><title>See Also</title>
<para>
<command>csv2ods</command>(1),
<command>odflint</command>(1)
</para>
</refsect1>

</refentry>
